⍝ Words to numbers, two ways: the same mapping as a case at level 0
⍝ and as a namespace at level 1.  One declaration serves both: `word`
⍝ is the type the case dispatches on and the segment type the paths
⍝ are made of (constructor names are global, so it could not be two).
⍝ The case is a few dozen atoms and returns a numeral; the namespace is
⍝ thousands, costs tens of thousands of contractions per lookup, and
⍝ returns an encoded term.  A namespace literal is an association list.
nat ≡ Zero | Suc nat
word ≡ One | Two | Three

⍝ level 0: case dispatch on the constructor; the result is a numeral
toNum w = w ▹ { One (Suc Zero); Two (Suc (Suc Zero)); Three (Suc (Suc (Suc Zero))) }
three ≔ toNum Three

term5 ≡ S | K | I | App term5 term5 | Scry
path ≡ Nil | Cons word path
bool ≡ PTrue | PFalse

oanswer ≡ OJust term5 | ONothing | ONotYet
outcome ≡ SteppedN term5 | DoneN | ErrdN | PendingN term5
result ≡ RValN term5 | RErrN | RTimeN | RBlockN term5

pAnd p q = p q PFalse
pKKF = K (K PFalse)
eqApp2P e t u t2 u2 = pAnd (e t t2) (e u u2)
eqApp1P e n t u = n PFalse PFalse PFalse (eqApp2P e t u) PFalse
eqNP e m n = (m (n PTrue  PFalse PFalse pKKF PFalse)
                (n PFalse PTrue  PFalse pKKF PFalse)
                (n PFalse PFalse PTrue  pKKF PFalse)
                (eqApp1P e n)
                (n PFalse PFalse PFalse pKKF PTrue))
EQ5 m = eqNP EQ5 m

scHitN rest v = SteppedN (rb v rest)

wfN e ≔ {
  stepScry1 p rest = e p (scHitN rest) ErrdN (PendingN p)
  stepScry args    = args DoneN (stepScry1 e)
}

⍝ level 1: the same facts as a namespace, read by the blocking interpreter
nums ≔ ns{/one ↦ <Suc Zero>, /two ↦ <Suc (Suc Zero)>, /three ↦ <Suc (Suc (Suc Zero))>}
n3 ≔ wfN nums ⊢ <∵/three>₁₀
